persona #self.first# practises a blessing in the length of one breath and listens for the roof birds to finish the pause.

words
oath! = Rattle my cheese board | Turn my stool to the damp
saying! = A short blessing reaches a long bench | Hear the quiet voice before filling the rafters
breathgap = a rest for breath | a little space in the response
cheese = a hard wedge | a clean-edged bit of cheese
roofbird = a pale-breasted hopper | a dust-brown roof bird
bellrope = the bell line | a long hanging rope
cloth = a plain wiping cloth | a square of linen
benchend = the narrow bench end | a corner of oak
mat = the rush runner | a strip of matting
doorlight = the broad doorlight | a rectangle of pale light
song = a measured answer | a sung response
rind = a tough rind | a hard cheese heel
cut = a narrow slice | a thin shaving
candlecup = a little metal cup | a plain clay holder
wax = a falling tear of wax | a hot wax bead
loft = the roof space | the dim upper beams
mist = a low roof mist | a fringe of damp air
step = a smooth step | a hollow doorstep
echo = an answering note | a faint high echo
dayglow = a touch of sun | a mild spring gleam
slate = a tilted slate | a dark little roof tile

any
opinion @1 church for 2 : There's a place in a service where a wolf can take the weight off one private hurt for a minute.
opinion @1 dole for 3 : Cheese and a little bread suffice for some prayers better than a second reading.
opinion @1 houses against 2 : I dread a quarrel between high benches that leaves the street to spend the winter in its shadow.
opinion @1 festivals for 2 : The first bell that puts a smile round a tired mouth has already done some good.
opinion @1 sump for 2 : I can pray with the low street under my paws as readily as the polished flags.
opinion @1 merchants against 1 : A portion for a hungry visitor should not be made smaller over three rounds of bargaining.
opinion @1 strangers for 1 : I can shift down a bench for a stranger who hasn't given a name.
opinion @1 road mixed 1 : Feet coming in off a rough road need a dry patch before anything is asked of them.
opinion @1 times against 1 [world.times=hard|lean] : Cold and hunger have grown loud in the response. We ought to listen before speaking over them.

grown
line @1 greet : Stand here in the clear strip of air. | A plain welcome and a place in the light.
line @1 greet.return : Welcome returned in my own quiet breath. | Glad your greeting carried so clearly.
line @1 again.open : Back before we've quite spent the pause.
line @1 farewell : Go out with room to breathe inside your coat. | May you take an easier pace on the homeward stones.
line @1 farewell.return : Your own breath stay free on the way. | That is a kind parting for a tired ear.
line @1 react.news : Let the account come through in the voice you first heard. | I can leave a proper silence for your news.
line @1 react.news.new : I hadn't heard even the echo of that.
line @1 react.news.known : Yes, that has sounded under these rafters before.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I'd leave a pause before giving that one an answer.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : Dear Bright One, give the hurting somewhere gentle to rest.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work] : A joyful sound, even when spoken very softly.
line @1 ask.how : Has the damp day taken much from your breathing?
line @1 answer.how : One breath after another. Some of them quite easy.
line @1 sympathise : I'll wait quietly beside you till the words have room.
line @1 reassure : An answer can come on the breath after the first one.
line @1 refuse : I have duties awaiting the little voice I've saved today.
line @1 accept_decline : There's no obligation to find a different answer for me.
line @1 preclose : I'd better spare one good breath for what's waiting.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go make what use you can of a quiet interval.
line @1 ack : Yes. I can hear the sense inside that.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : A place for an unfamiliar face beside an ordinary wolf.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : A little new light to share before the street grows loud.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends] : That voice could find me under any height of roof.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : Come just this side, where the air moves freely!
line @1 thank : My breath comes easier for your help. I am grateful.
line @1 deflect_thanks : You came when I had a little steadiness worth sharing.
line @1 give.advice : Reach for dry wood before you trust all your weight.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : The work is moving. I've one clear moment for your words.
line @2 ask.how [pair.band=friends] : Have you had a chance to let a difficult day go quiet?
line @4 greet [here.time=night] : A late arrival may still have the lamp's better side.
scene exchange1
when topic=faith self.job=priest
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I fit the shortest blessing into one clean breath. | I give the congregation a little space after each answer.
b : What if the breath catches? | Do you forget the words?
a : Then I speak the last word slowly on the next. | I remember that somebody else may need longer over them.

scene exchange2
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Damp puts a little catch into my best speaking voice. | I turn my head during the longest response.
b : Was that a cough just now? | To hear the back bench?
a : Only the pause taking rather more sound than usual. | Partly. And sometimes a throat deserves a discreet corner.

scene exchange3
when topic=food self.likes=hard_cheese
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A hard cheese pares into very thin pieces. | I save the rough rind for the end.
b : Are you saving it? | A reward for eating the rest?
a : I like a little taste that asks me to take time. | It lets me sit chewing awhile longer in peace.

scene exchange4
when topic=pastimes self.likes=roof_birds
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Roof birds go quiet for one heartbeat when a door bangs. | I watch for the bird that stays when the others lift.
b : Are you counting heartbeats? | Why that one?
a : I'm waiting for their shoulders to come down with mine. | Courage and good balance can look much alike at a distance.

scene exchange5
when topic=season self.likes=first_warm_day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My voice knows the first mild day before my coat knows it. | I like a first warm afternoon on bare stone.
b : A stronger voice? | Does it hold the sun?
a : A longer breath without any scratch along the edge. | Long enough to lean against it after a service.

scene exchange6
when topic=pastimes self.likes=festival_bells
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A festival bell seems to rise at the end. | The last festival bell leaves people talking in louder voices.
b : Does the note change? | Do you mind the noise?
a : My chin goes up. That's probably where the lifting happens. | No. Some kinds of volume come from a happy surprise.

scene exchange7
when topic=prices self.dislikes=haggling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I find haggling tiring before the first figure's finished. | Three voices arguing over a wedge of cheese spoil its taste in my head.
b : Do you accept any price? | Do you go without?
a : I look for a plain one that fits my purse. | I save the purchase for a quieter counter.

scene exchange8
when topic=home self.dislikes=wet_floors
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put the first mat where wet paws actually land. | Wet stone shines beautifully until one's foot slides.
b : And the second? | Do you prefer it dull?
a : No second one. I move the first when I'm wrong. | I prefer getting to choose when I kneel.

scene exchange9
when topic=family self.married=yes self.spouse
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep the truest answer about my breathing for #self.spouse#. | A small silence beside #self.spouse# does me as much good as a whole high window.
b : Why only there? | Just sitting together?
a : It's easier to be plain in a familiar room. | That is a fairly considerable thing.

scene exchange10
when topic=work self.job=priest self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# the nearest wall sends a quick answer back. | I test a speaking place with a soft ordinary word.
b : Does the echo get in the way? | Before a prayer?
a : If I speak too fast, I end up talking over myself. | I want the listener farthest from me to hear a blessing the first time.

scene exchange11
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : After my cough, I trust the Bright One with even a word that's half swallowed. | I don't think a quiet prayer counts for less.
b : Even if the congregation misses it? | Why lift the voice at all?
a : A wolf can ask me to repeat it. The Bright One won't need to. | So the wolf praying beside me can find where the words join.

scene exchange12
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I heard #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I'm letting the words rest a bit. | A rumour dances very nicely on an echo.
b : For how long? | What does that prove?
a : Until repeating those words might comfort somebody instead of causing hurt. | That a room has hard walls. Nothing about the matter itself.

scene exchange13
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Lean days put a thin edge on the singing. | When supper's short I shorten the reading before it.
b : Are fewer wolves coming? | For impatience?
a : I can't say that. I hear tiredness in some of the voices. | For hunger. They need a different response.

scene exchange14
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'm afraid the Houses may lose patience with each other before winter. | I'd like a service with both doors open in winter.
b : Are you announcing a quarrel? | Wouldn't that chill the room?
a : No. A fear of mine shouldn't arrive in somebody else's ears dressed as news. | In my imagining every visitor brings enough warmth to make the draught worthwhile.

scene exchange15
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The streets climbing out of the Sump require a different pace from a prayer. | I like the roofs seen from the first bend up the hill.
b : A quicker pace? | The better houses?
a : A slower one, if I'm to have breath enough on arrival. | All the roofs. The low ones make a grand place for a small bird.

scene exchange16
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I break an uphill journey into phrases. | I come down a hill looking for wet flags.
b : Do you say them aloud? | Skidded before?
a : I keep the punctuation under my breath until the steep bit ends. | Twice. Once ought to teach a wolf, but wet stone finds me a slow pupil.

scene exchange17
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I remember the first response I ever heard quite clearly. | I was once too proud to stop and clear my throat.
b : What did it say? | What happened?
a : I remember somebody making space to let my voice come through. | The next words came out like gravel. I let the pause do its honest work now.

scene exchange18
when topic=work self.job=priest
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep a plain cloth beside the lectern. | I let the last listener choose how long a greeting lasts.
b : For the damp? | What if you both fall silent?
a : For any wolf needing it. It gets less remarkable that way. | We have made a perfectly good beginning.

scene exchange19
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I listen to the street before I decide how loudly to speak. | I shut a door by its handle before I set a book down.
b : Are you competing with it? | So the words won't blow away?
a : Trying to find the gap the carts aren't using. | So nobody's prayer ends in a bang.

scene exchange20
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I warm my hands across my throat before a long reading. | A cold neck makes me read in short phrases.
b : Does the warmth travel inward? | Is that a disadvantage?
a : Enough that I remember the body has to carry the words. | A short phrase gives a listener a decent foothold sometimes.

scene exchange21
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An unfamiliar wolf may choose the end seat. | I give a late arrival the nod I wanted when I was new.
b : May want to leave early? | Which nod?
a : May want to stay without having to climb over anybody first. | One that means sit down in peace and nobody's counting the minutes.

scene exchange22
when topic=food self.likes=hard_cheese
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can tell well-aged cheese by the way a corner breaks. | I put cheese in a separate twist of cloth.
b : Straight across? | To keep the taste out of the bread?
a : A rough little cliff face with crystals in it. | To keep the tiny crumbs in my possession.

scene exchange23
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep the shelf with my books on the dry side. | I turn a rush mat over to dry it.
b : Which side stays safest in a shower? | Both sides evenly?
a : The paste softens where the wall's been damp. I inspect the least important spine. | If I don't, the damp underneath gets the last word.

scene exchange24
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd let #self.friend# hear a prayer while I'm still trying out the words. | A friend can tell my best voice from my bravest one.
b : Even the pauses? | Which gets louder?
a : Especially those. It helps me hear where the person listening needs a breath. | The brave one. The best one doesn't have to prove itself.

scene exchange25
when topic=work self.job=priest
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I don't let the whole service depend on my longest note. | I reserve space in my notes for a plain word after a formal one.
b : Does the note sometimes fail? | Is one better?
a : What's being said deserves to outlast one throat's best effort. | The second gives any lost listener a chance to find the way again.

scene exchange26
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can hear the damp in the first sound off the wall. | Rain finds the lowest groove on the flags.
b : Is that why you swallowed? | Do you put a bucket there?
a : That and trying to speak before I'd finished listening. | I put the mat where the next foot would otherwise find it.

scene exchange27
when topic=pastimes self.likes=roof_birds
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a bird that studies the edge before hopping over. | A bird's claws make a surprisingly clear tick on tile.
b : Are you fond of caution? | Can you tell which bird?
a : It's easier to call a small pause sensible when it belongs to another creature. | Only that one has gone and another hasn't followed yet.

scene exchange28
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've never prayed for a thunderous voice. | I set my light where a weary face can look away from it.
b : But you want to be heard? | Is that part of a service?
a : Clearly. Thunder doesn't always say the words one wants to hear. | It's part of sharing one small flame in a roomful of faces.

scene exchange29
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I reckon the cost of a meal in the time spent arranging it. | I take small change loose in a pocket.
b : Not only the coin? | A habit for offerings?
a : A hungry wolf has already paid plenty in waiting. | For a purchase that ought to be done without a dozen counters looking on.

scene exchange30
when topic=season
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The autumn air feels thin before the roof birds depart. | Winter makes me put a warm cloth by the door before I go out.
b : Are you sorry about winter? | Ready for your return?
a : I'm sorry to see a good pair of wings leave a good patch of tile. | Ready if somebody colder walks in ahead of me.

story tale1 [topic=work self.job=priest]
  : I tried a reading in an empty room and timed my pauses with drops from the eaves. I had an elegant arrangement worked out.
  : When the rain stopped, I stood waiting in perfect silence for the next line.
  b : Who gave you the cue?
  : A bird finally shook a drop off a branch. I finished the passage and resolved to keep my time with breathing things.

story tale2 [topic=pastimes self.likes=roof_birds]
  : A roof bird shook a feather loose and it drifted straight down the shaft of light over my book. I followed it with great solemnity.
  : It landed on the word I'd stopped at, which struck me as a courteous piece of assistance.
  b : Did you keep it for a marker?
  : I took it outside. A clean slip of paper does the work and catches fewer breaths on the way.

story tale3 [topic=food self.likes=hard_cheese]
  : I shaved a piece of cheese so thin the window shone through it. One little bright patch looked just like the door standing open after a service.
  : I put it on my bread, meaning to admire the picture another minute.
  b : Did it still look like a door?
  : The light went out the instant it touched the crust. I ate that little door with an entirely clear conscience.

story tale4 [topic=memories]
  : I used to carry a spare scrap of a reading in case I forgot the middle. I copied it out in a cramped hand on very thin paper.
  : The first time I actually needed the scrap the words were too small to read in decent light.
  b : Did the middle stay forgotten?
  : I said in plain words what the missing passage meant. Nobody was left without the sense of it. I copy in a wider hand now.

story tale5 [topic=faith]
  : I cleared my throat softly before a blessing and startled myself with the voice that rose from my chest. It rose right up under the rafters.
  : I stopped, waiting for the echo to settle back down.
  b : Did the prayer lose its way?
  : No. For the first time I noticed how the pause gave the other voices a place to join in.

rule @call1
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=priest
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A little clear space for the last response. | The far bench wants to hear these words too.

rule @call2
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The mat needs moving over another hand's breadth. | Damp doing the talking behind my voice.

rule @call3
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say First light finds dry stone above the drip. | Hush, there's a roof bird calling ahead of the bell.

rule @call4
when concept=bark self.likes=festival_bells
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Give the last bell room to finish ringing. | That note could lift a dozen lowered chins.

rule @call5
when concept=bark self.likes=hard_cheese
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A thin slice and a moment to chew. | A little cheese goes a good way after a service.

rule @call6
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Leave the lower light burning a moment. | Evening voices needn't strain to fill the roof.

dlg @1 resident.hub : I've a quieter spot at my elbow, even if the street outside is noisy.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, your voice is clear to me over the sound of the rafters.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : A quiet word suits this late hour very well.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : I'll give your words a hearing without raising mine.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=priest] : I lead prayers at #self.workplace#. I keep weary voices in mind when choosing the responses.
dlg @2 resident.job : I've done a good turn when somebody breathes easier after my turn at the reading.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : This is the news that reached my ears. #world.news#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : I have heard that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Let us handle somebody else's reputation with care.
dlg @1 resident.bye : May the Bright One grant you a sheltered seat once your errand's done.
dlg @1 church.greet [here.day=rest] : On this Restday our service is #here.service#. There's a place for another voice.
dlg @2 church.greet [here.day!=rest] : Come into the quieter air. There's room for a question about the service.
dlg @1 church.service [here.day=rest] : The service today is #here.service#. Come in at whatever pace your breath allows.
dlg @2 church.service [here.day!=rest] : There are prayers enough for an ordinary day. The full service has its own day of rest.
dlg @1 church.poor : A meal left for a hungry wolf does a great deal of speaking of its own.
dlg @1 church.offering : An offering ought to come freely and leave the giver able to eat.
dlg @1 church.thanked : I am grateful. A hungry mouth will have better cause to be grateful still.
dlg @1 church.bye : Walk lightly where the flags have kept a little damp.
graft resident.hub
choice Why leave a gap in a blessing? -> roof_response
node roof_response
say The words are meant to leave my mouth and find the farthest wolf in the room. They need a moment to arrive before the next lot come after them.
free
choice And if nobody answers? -> roof_response_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node roof_response_again
say A quiet listener has still taken part. I listen also, and let the words find their own way home.
choice I'll give the pause a moment. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye

graft church.greet
choice Is a short prayer enough? [self.job=priest] -> short_blessing
node short_blessing
say A wolf may have only a few words in a hard hour. I believe those few come through with perfect clarity to the Bright One.
free
choice What if the voice catches? -> short_blessing_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node short_blessing_again
say Then breathe first. Your prayer can wait in the quiet for the second breath.
choice Let the room grow quiet again. -> greet
choice Goodbye. -> bye
